id: pm-rust-ufzy
title: Extend native list parity to pagination and bounded output contracts
description: "Follow-up to pm-rust-p0no: current compatibility mode explicitly requires unbounded amount and cost. Implement limits, cursors, continuation fingerprints and output budgeting with full-envelope golden tests against the exact published PM CLI. Keep 100 percent coverage and maintainer publication guard."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: conformance,read-parity,rust
created_at: "2026-10-02T19:11:02.190Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-06T12:44:01.018Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: Real TS and Rust CLIs match multi-page envelopes and continuation fingerprints on shared fixtures; Stale or mismatched cursors fail consistently; No item loss or repeated rows; Output omission and budget receipts match; Existing gates remain enforced
parent: pm-rust-u4al
comments[46]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-02T20:09:16.243Z",codex-sol,"PR #58 full-projection follow-up: published --full additionally emits read_output alias/migration/budget diagnostics, including estimated_tokens. Native --full restores complete metadata with unchanged selection, but these output-policy diagnostics remain outside the current slice and are explicitly documented. Synthetic exact published read_output receipt captured in tests/fixtures/list-full-read-output-2026-10-2.json; original nine envelope comparisons remain exact and unchanged. Include full-projection output policy in this bounded-output/canonical-controls follow-up."
  "2026-10-05T07:13:33.482Z",codex-sol,"Inspect the published 2026.10.5 list contract and existing differential fixtures before implementing native pagination, cursor validation and bounded projection receipts. Preserve every existing release gate; add shared-fixture differential and randomized page-walk evidence."
  "2026-10-05T07:38:18.064Z",codex-sol,"Baseline: all eight existing list differential tests pass with the installed TS CLI 2026.10.5, including nine golden envelopes. Contract discovery: --after follows item identity and collapses subsequent envelope metadata into continuation_contract; it does not bind a snapshot. --output-cursor binds the projected row collection and rejects stale snapshots. Pagination tests will distinguish these contracts instead of claiming producer cursors refuse mutations."
  "2026-10-05T08:09:45.528Z",codex-sol,"Implemented producer paging, snapshot output continuations, full-output diagnostics and core triage budgets in the CLI and Workspace::list_page. Differential comparisons use complete stdout/stderr bytes and fixed clocks, with no field normalization. Original nine unbounded goldens remain unchanged on 2026.10.5. Additional tests exposed canonical-plus-legacy receipt precedence and final-page rebasing; both now have regression cases. Changelog regenerated via just changelog-full: unchanged because the documented generator selects closed items and this task must remain open."
  "2026-10-05T08:21:26.474Z",codex-sol,"Resume verification: producer and budget page walks match both published 2026.10.5 and native CLIs, including exact receipts. Concurrent mutation is now exercised through a separate native update process. Unicode surrogate-splitting compaction has a reproduced serialization gap tracked separately in pm-rust-8hkb; this task remains open pending orchestrator verification. Coverage gates remain at 100 percent in all four dimensions."
  "2026-10-05T08:25:52.357Z",codex-sol,The first pm-linked differential run passed the eight existing list tests but exceeded its default 120-second runner timeout while the pagination suite was still running under concurrent gate load. Raised only the runner timeout to 600 seconds; assertions and coverage thresholds remain unchanged. A fresh linked run will provide the final receipt.
  "2026-10-05T08:28:47.061Z",codex-sol,"Final PM-linked differential receipt passed: all eight existing list tests and all six pagination tests, including 96 randomized SDK page walks and separate-process stale snapshot mutation. Full all-targets/all-features suite also passed 178 tests. Clippy and private/public rustdoc gates passed. Instrumented four-metric coverage is still being measured; no 100-percent result is claimed yet."
  "2026-10-05T08:38:05.644Z",codex-sol,"Coverage gate initially refused the implementation at 99.48 percent lines, 98.80 functions, 99.34 regions and 97.85 branches. Added meaningful direct-SDK refusal and multiple nested collection compaction tests, plus existing/final producer cursor rebasing checks. The expanded 181-test suite and deny-warning clippy pass; fresh instrumented coverage is running with the same four 100-percent thresholds."
  "2026-10-05T08:54:07.569Z",codex-sol,"Final just release-check passed on the implemented source: 183 ordinary and instrumented tests; 2892/2892 lines, 251/251 functions, 4383/4383 regions, 604/604 branches. Formatting, deny-warning clippy, private/public rustdoc, dependency audit and generated changelog check passed. PM-linked real-CLI differential run passed all 15 tests including 96 randomized page walks. Original nine unbounded goldens remain unchanged. Full Unicode-boundary parity is deferred to pm-rust-8hkb, so the PR will remain draft and this item stays open. The unchanged lock-replacement fixture had one intermittent failure, passed isolated and aggregate retries, and is tracked in pm-rust-ax0o."
  "2026-10-05T08:56:50.536Z",codex-sol,"Implementation committed as 5ecc383 and published in draft PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/60. Verification receipt is recorded in docs/LIST_PAGINATION_2026_10_5.md. Release gate and all four coverage metrics pass; original goldens remain unchanged. Full parity remains incomplete at the surrogate-splitting boundary tracked in pm-rust-8hkb; pm-rust-ax0o tracks the observed legacy fixture race. No items are closed, and the claim is being released for orchestrator review."
  "2026-10-05T09:04:46.450Z",codex-sol,"Windows CI follow-up: full run 37287014816 log retrieved. All three failures first differ inside producer next_cursor fingerprints; preceding rows, row counts and after-id/index values match. Budget snapshot continuation and stale-refusal tests pass on Windows. Investigating canonical tracker-root representation in the native query hash before changing product or harness; no tests will be skipped and no GitHub replies will be posted."
  "2026-10-05T09:10:28.973Z",codex-sol,"Root cause confirmed as a native product bug, not a fixture artifact: Rust canonicalize adds the Windows verbatim namespace prefix to pmRoot; published SDK resolvePmRoot uses Node path.resolve/path.join and hashes the ordinary drive or UNC spelling. All three Windows failures first differ inside next_cursor.fingerprint after identical rows/counts; snapshot cursors do not hash pmRoot and pass. Native query hashing now strips only the namespace prefix, preserving backslashes and filesystem paths. Portable drive/UNC regression tests include a hash measured with the actual published 2026.10.5 SDK. Differential harness and Windows test selection remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-05T09:13:59.395Z",codex-sol,"Local Windows-fix verification passed: just release-check completed all 184 tests in ordinary and instrumented runs, formatting, deny-warning clippy, private/public rustdoc, dependency and identity audit, pinned changelog verification. Coverage remains 100 percent: lines 2897/2897, functions 252/252, regions 4392/4392, branches 606/606. pm test pm-rust-ufzy --run --progress passed both linked commands: 15 real-CLI differential tests including randomized page walks, and 4 pagination unit tests including the new drive/UNC regression. Preparing the focused product fix for PR #60; Windows CI verification is next."
  "2026-10-05T09:21:21.060Z",codex-sol,"The first focused namespace fix passed local release-check and CI ubuntu/macOS/aggregate, but Windows run 37288712120 still fails at producer query fingerprints. Namespace removal alone is insufficient. Adding failure-only path-shape diagnostics (separator counts, case-insensitive equality, canonical equality and first differing character codes), without storing or logging paths, to identify the remaining Windows representation difference. All byte assertions remain intact."
  "2026-10-05T09:30:12.649Z",codex-sol,"Windows diagnostic evidence from run 37289539548: native canonical-root spelling has length 61 and no short-name alias; Node resolved-root spelling has length 58 and an 8.3 alias. Both use eight backslashes and zero forward slashes, so separator or budgeting changes cannot fix the difference. The product now retains resolved discovery spelling for query hashes separately from its canonical filesystem root. Temporary diagnostic instrumentation is removed and original exact byte assertions restored. New cross-platform discovery tests cover workspace, nested directory, file and direct tracker starts, plus typed empty-path refusal; no Windows tests are disabled."
  "2026-10-05T09:34:18.043Z",codex-sol,"Complete product fix is committed as 889e4bf and pushed to PR #60. Final just release-check passed 186 tests in ordinary and instrumented runs with all four coverage metrics at 100 percent, plus formatting, clippy, complete rustdoc, identity/dependency audit and pinned changelog check. pm test pm-rust-ufzy --run --progress passed all three linked commands: 15 real-CLI differential tests, 4 pagination unit tests, 3 workspace unit tests. Original differential harness is restored and no Windows tests are skipped. Watching Windows job in run 37290744982 to verify the complete namespace and short-alias correction."
  "2026-10-05T09:36:48.532Z",codex-sol,"Run 37290744982 exposed a macOS SDK-only regression from applying lexical spelling to every OS: CLI-to-CLI byte comparisons pass, but the SDK supplied temp-root alias hashes differently from the physical process working directory. Preserving Unix canonical query spelling restores previous SDK behavior; Windows query spelling remains resolved without short-name expansion. Portable tests exercise both platform choices directly, and every differential test still runs on Windows. Full release gate is being rerun for this correction."
  "2026-10-05T09:37:39.629Z",codex-sol,"Windows verification succeeded: Rust windows-latest in run 37290744982 passed the full suite, including all three previously failing pagination comparisons. This confirms that preserving the resolved short-name spelling and removing Rust namespace syntax fixes the native Windows divergence. Applying the resolved spelling only on Windows also restores the established Unix SDK/CLI path contract; final correction and receipts will be pushed after the refreshed local gate."
  "2026-10-05T09:40:07.089Z",codex-sol,"Final platform correction passed just release-check: 187 tests in ordinary and instrumented runs; formatting, clippy, complete docs, identity/dependency audit, pinned changelog check all pass. Coverage stays 100 percent: lines 2928/2928, functions 256/256, regions 4427/4427, branches 610/610. pm test pm-rust-ufzy --run --progress passed all three exact linked commands (15 differential, 4 pagination unit, 4 workspace unit). Windows source fix was verified green in run 37290744982. Final commit preserves Unix canonical spelling and the verified Windows resolved spelling, then rechecks CI on the final head. Releasing claim and leaving the item open for orchestrator verification and the previously tracked boundaries; no GitHub replies or test exclusions were introduced."
  "2026-10-05T09:54:12.434Z",codex-sol,"Review follow-up on head 78068d9: reading findings 4182703846, 4182703859, 4182703871 and 4182703906 in full, then reproducing each against the actual published TS CLI before choosing fixes or rejections. Add regression assertions that fail on revert, preserve every gate and all platform tests, record differential and coverage receipts. No GitHub replies will be posted."
  "2026-10-05T10:07:40.684Z",codex-sol,"Real reference evidence: TS 2026.10.5 and native have byte-identical combined-cap failures (50-row snapshot hashed after amount cap, unchanged replay stale; producer limit 50/output limit 30 rebases using capped count and skips rows after deletion). Preserving pinned parity is the default pending user steering. Float divergence confirmed with metadata 1e20: native prints exponent form, TS prints decimal; row counts and snapshot hashes differ, and native rejects the TS cursor as stale. 30.0 itself is normalized to integer by current TOON decoding, so regression also includes actual surviving float metadata. Equals-form controls also differ in refusal receipts. Number formatting must be shared across hashes, wire JSON and token estimates to fix the full float envelope."
  "2026-10-05T11:04:46.424Z",pi-rust-greptile2,"Continuing the head-78068d9 review follow-up and taking over the stale claim. Prior differential evidence is confirmed against the installed TS 2026.10.5: findings 4182703846 and 4182703859 reproduce byte-identically in the published reference (snapshot hashed after the amount cap with stale unchanged replay; producer rebasing uses the capped count after deletion), so they are pinned as reference parity with new differential tests rather than diverging fixes. 4182703871 and 4182703906 are real divergences: shared JS-compatible number formatting (ryu-js) now covers history hashes, snapshot hashes, wire JSON and token estimates, and equals-form native controls are stripped from recovery. Re-verified against the real TS CLI: float values match byte-for-byte (30.0 as 30, 1e20 as 100000000000000000000, 1e-6 as 0.000001). Also confirmed native sorts extra metadata keys while the reference preserves file order — a pre-existing separate divergence that will be filed as a follow-up item, out of this slice."
  "2026-10-05T11:56:54.251Z",pi-rust-greptile2,"Coverage-gate follow-up: the first instrumented run of the JS number-formatting fix reported one uncovered region in the CLI response writer. Root cause: the to_value error region of the generic writer could only be exercised by a synthetic test-only serialization type, and the region summary never counted that record. The response writer now serializes through a shared JavaScript-number formatter (serde_json Serializer with a custom Formatter; pretty layout identical to the reference), which restores the original writer-error topology and removes the to_value intermediate entirely. A wire-bytes equivalence test asserts the writer's output equals the shared renderer plus newline. Instrumented aggregate now reports 100 percent on all four metrics: 3036/3036 lines, 273/273 functions, 4605/4605 regions, 624/624 branches, with all 197 tests passing including the byte-exact differential suite."
  "2026-10-05T11:56:59.676Z",pi-rust-greptile2,"Coverage-gate follow-up: the first instrumented run of the JS number-formatting fix reported one uncovered region in the CLI response writer. The to_value error region of the generic writer could only be exercised by a synthetic test-only serialization type, and the region summary never counted that record. The response writer now serializes through a shared JavaScript-number formatter (a serde_json Serializer with a custom Formatter whose pretty layout matches the reference), which restores the original writer-error topology and removes the to_value intermediate. A wire-bytes equivalence test asserts the writer output equals the shared renderer plus newline. Instrumented aggregate now reports 100 percent on all four metrics: 3036/3036 lines, 273/273 functions, 4605/4605 regions, 624/624 branches, with all 197 tests passing including the byte-exact differential suite."
  "2026-10-06T10:45:15.164Z",pi-glm,"Taking over the stale claim from the finished number-formatting slice to handle CodeRabbit findings 4184061254 and 4184061258. Will reproduce the legacy after-cursor final-page triage compaction against the installed TS CLI before deciding whether native diverges, and will make the cursor-refusal argument publisher use args_os so non-UTF-8 arguments cannot panic."
  "2026-10-06T10:58:03.080Z",pi-glm,"Finding 4184061254 reproduced against published PM CLI 2026.10.5; the installed 2026.10.6 context-intent decoder is identical. A 75-item triage page with limit 69 produced a producer cursor at after_index 68. Stripping after_index and requesting the final page with --for triage --token-budget 800 --full made native compact three rows and write after_index 3. The reference omitted the page with budget_exceeded effective_budget_infeasible and did not rebase. Deleting the rebased identity then resumed at demo-0015 and repeated earlier rows. Native now requires after_index before compaction, matching the reference omission. The unit regression legacy_final_page_without_after_index_does_not_rebase_from_zero fails when that requirement is removed. The differential legacy_after_without_after_index_omits_final_triage_page pins the published omission. No upstream issue: the reference does not rebase from zero. The remaining continuation_contract.fingerprint gap is tracked in pm-rust-poen and is not changed in this slice."
  "2026-10-06T11:06:12.506Z",pi-glm,"Finding 4184061258: cursor refusals read std::env::args_os and lossily own each argument, so a non-UTF-8 argument cannot panic the JSON refusal. The envelope still exits 2. Unix unit test non_utf8_arguments_publish_the_cursor_refusal_envelope publishes a non-UTF-8 OsString inside that envelope. Process test non_utf8_workspace_argument_refuses_a_bad_cursor_without_panic exits 2; reverting the call site to env::args panics with exit 101 and fails that test. Windows CI does not construct invalid OsStrings. Local just release-check passed after the decode-failure coverage fix: formatting, deny-warning clippy, private and public rustdoc, full suite, 100 percent lines functions regions and branches (3046/3046, 274/274, 4616/4616, 624/624), cargo audit, and pinned changelog check."
  "2026-10-06T11:45:23.132Z",codex-sol,"Continuation review by codex-sol: inspected all inherited code, tests, documentation and tracker changes; retaining the after_index compaction guard, args_os publisher, Unix regression tests, and separate pm-rust-poen fingerprint follow-up. git pull --ff-only was already current. Will independently reproduce against installed TS CLI, prove regressions fail on revert, run release-check and tracker tests, commit fixes, merge origin/main as required by the continuation, push and monitor PR 60 checks. No GitHub replies or issue filing."
  "2026-10-06T11:46:39.317Z",codex-sol,"Independent differential reproduction against installed TS CLI 2026.10.6 confirms finding 4184061254 is a native divergence: a 75-row fixture, producer limit 69, stripped after_index, triage token-budget 800 and --full yields native after_index 3 with rows, while TS omits rows with effective_budget_infeasible. Retaining the required-after_index fix, with no upstream issue draft needed. The legacy_final_page_without_after_index_does_not_rebase_from_zero unit test fails against HEAD before the fix (exit 101)."
  "2026-10-06T11:47:41.871Z",codex-sol,"The existing CI matrix ran functional tests on Linux/macOS/Windows but measured coverage only on Linux. Extended the release-check job to the same three operating systems with Bash shell defaults and fail-fast disabled; no thresholds or test exclusions changed. All platforms must independently pass the existing four-metric 100 percent coverage predicate. Findings regression reverts were restored; env::args caused the process test to observe exit 101 and panic, proving the args_os fix is necessary."
  "2026-10-06T11:50:04.859Z",codex-sol,"All nine focused linked tests passed. The first aggregate run was interrupted by the linked runner default 120-second timeout during instrumented pagination tests, with no assertion failure. Increased only this linked command timeout to 600 seconds and rerunning it. PM health and validate return ok with existing advisory warnings; no unrelated tracker reconciliation performed."
  "2026-10-06T11:52:28.696Z",codex-sol,"Local verification complete: all nine focused linked tests passed; pm test pm-rust-ufzy --run --progress --only-index 10 --timeout 600 passed just release-check in 127 seconds against pinned TS CLI 2026.10.5. Coverage is 3046/3046 lines, 274/274 functions, 4616/4616 regions and 624/624 branches, all 100 percent. Formatting, deny-warning clippy, private documentation, full tests, cargo audit and changelog check passed. Independently confirmed the fixed omission receipt matches installed TS 2026.10.6. Both finding regression tests fail on revert. Next: commit, merge origin/main action-pin updates, push, and check remote matrix coverage."
  "2026-10-06T11:56:25.325Z",codex-sol,"CI follow-up: Linux functional tests and the aggregate release gate passed at 829e3a5. macOS rejected creation of the process-test non-UTF-8 directory with Illegal byte sequence before dispatch. Scoped that filesystem-dependent black-box regression to Linux, where it proves the original panic; the invalid OsString unit test still runs on every Unix platform, including macOS. No production code or coverage threshold changed. Windows gates are still running. Rechecking and pushing this fixture portability correction."
  "2026-10-06T12:01:26.377Z",codex-sol,"At 62e04c6, functional CI tests pass on Linux/macOS/Windows and the Linux aggregate gate passes. The newly enabled macOS aggregate fails its 100 percent coverage predicate after all tests pass; its log prints only false, with no uncovered locations. Added totals and missing-line reporting on predicate failure to just release-check, preserving the threshold and exit failure, to diagnose the actual platform gap. Windows aggregate is still running."
  "2026-10-06T12:08:05.703Z",codex-sol,"Coverage diagnostic at 282d5cd confirms the macOS gap is exactly src/mutation.rs lines 644-647 and 908-911: history flush and parent sync error mapping. Added null-device failure cases on Unix and the Windows NUL device to the existing unit tests; both portable additions pass on Linux. No product code or coverage threshold changed. The full local aggregate rerun is still active. Will push these test corrections and verify the final platform matrix."
  "2026-10-06T12:09:08.979Z",codex-sol,"Final implementation receipt: portable mutation error tests pass locally, including both newly linked pm test commands. The full just release-check rerun passed in 232 seconds and still measures 100 percent lines, functions, regions and branches. Finding 4184061254 is fixed native divergence from installed TS 2026.10.6 and pinned TS 2026.10.5; finding 4184061258 is fixed with args_os and lossy argument publication. Regression tests fail on revert. Commits so far: bedc7a3 fixes, 829e3a5 origin/main merge, 62e04c6 macOS fixture correction, 282d5cd coverage diagnostics. pm-rust-poen stays open for legacy fingerprint parity. Implementation work is finished; releasing the claim for orchestrator review while passively monitoring the next pushed CI matrix. No item closed, GitHub issue filed, bot mentioned, or GitHub reply sent."
  "2026-10-06T12:12:29.280Z",codex-sol,"Compatibility check found main branch protection requires the exact status name Release gate aggregate. Preserved that existing name for the Linux matrix entry while naming the macOS and Windows entries separately. Matrix scope, checks, thresholds, test commands and source code are unchanged. This prevents an otherwise green matrix from leaving the required status absent. Releasing the claim after this workflow correction."
  "2026-10-06T12:22:14.940Z",codex-sol,"PR #60 Windows aggregate coverage: inspect the failed run, add Windows-native symlink, surrogate-name, filesystem failure and lock-contention fixtures beside Unix tests, then verify Windows compilation and Linux release-check before pushing. Keep all coverage thresholds and reachable error handling intact; at most three CI rounds."
  "2026-10-06T12:24:56.494Z",codex-sol,"Failed run 37461636884 confirms mutation lines 457,466,556,564-566,604-606,737,1278,1296-1300 and workspace lines 98,176-178,370. main.rs has one missed region, zero missed lines, so show-missing-lines supplies no main line; the OsString argument closure is exercised only by the Unix fixture. Added native surrogate-name cases, exclusive file handles, a real NTFS temporary-name overflow, file/directory symlinks with mandatory CI privilege enforcement, and a verbatim parent-component path."
  "2026-10-06T12:26:03.681Z",codex-sol,"Windows all-targets check and Rust 1.90 Windows all-targets/all-features Clippy passed. First Linux release-check stopped at the pinned-oracle assertion: globally installed PM CLI is 2026.10.6 but this branch requires 2026.10.5. Installing the exact oracle inside the package worktree and rerunning with explicit PM_NODE_CLI; no package source or thresholds changed."
  "2026-10-06T12:29:52.475Z",codex-sol,"Local validation passed through pm test: Windows cargo check all-targets; Rust 1.90 Windows Clippy all-targets/all-features with warnings denied; mutation unit tests; read_contract tests; just release-check against the installed 2026.10.5 oracle. Linux measured lines/functions/regions/branches = 100/100/100/100. Dispositions: mutation 457 parentless root; 466 and 556 real surrogate filenames; 564-566 NTFS temporary-name overflow; 604-606 exclusive replacement-target handle; 737 exclusive second lock handle; 1278 file/directory symlinks; 1296-1300 exclusive item handle. workspace 98 verbatim parent-component fixture; 176-178 exclusive item handle; 370 real nested symlinks. main missed region receives Windows OsString surrogate arguments; the original report has no missed main lines. Proceeding with CI round 1."
  "2026-10-06T12:33:54.527Z",codex-sol,"CI round 1 at 7a5aabf: Linux aggregate passed. macOS failed because the added file creation for Unix invalid-byte names is rejected by APFS; restore Unix input-only fixtures and keep actual surrogate files on Windows. Windows unit tests confirmed the publisher and symlink fixtures pass, but exclusive incumbent reads yield sharing violation rather than PermissionDenied, and real verbatim parent paths reach the fold then canonicalize refuses with error 123. Correct those two assertions with a pending-delete handle fixture and explicit typed InvalidFilename refusal; no production changes."
  "2026-10-06T12:35:24.114Z",codex-sol,Round 1 follow-up pm-rust-wshr records the exclusive incumbent sharing-violation classification for investigation outside this coverage-only task. Windows parent fixture now asserts error 123 after folding the real parent component and verifies ordinary spelling discovers the tracker; Windows surrogate files remain real while Unix fixtures preserve their existing input-only behavior.
  "2026-10-06T12:36:47.727Z",codex-sol,"Round 1 completed: Linux aggregate passed; macOS and Windows aggregates failed during the ordinary test phase, before coverage reporting. Corrected all reported fixture failures. Windows check and strict Clippy passed again. Linux just release-check passed again through pm test with 100/100/100/100 against oracle 2026.10.5. Starting CI round 2; retain the separate sharing-violation investigation in pm-rust-wshr."
  "2026-10-06T12:41:54.825Z",codex-sol,"CI round 2 at f167758: Linux aggregate passed; macOS ordinary matrix tests passed; Windows unit suite passed 89/90, with only a fixture overconstraint: the real pending-delete read returns NotFound rather than PermissionDenied. Both are explicitly supported contention presentations. Accept either read error, verify retained handle metadata, and still require the contender to return LockConflict and acquisition to succeed after handle release. Preparing final permitted CI round 3."
  "2026-10-06T12:44:00.509Z",codex-sol,"Final local gate before CI round 3 passed through pm test: just release-check with pinned oracle 2026.10.5 remains 100/100/100/100; Windows all-targets check and strict Rust 1.90 Clippy passed. Round 2 finished with both Linux and macOS aggregates passing, Windows failing only the pending-delete read-kind assertion before coverage. Final fixture accepts exactly NotFound or PermissionDenied, proves the second handle still owns three real bytes, requires LockConflict while held, and requires successful acquisition after release. All original coverage gaps retain their native fixtures; no source or thresholds changed. Release the claim without closing; the final permitted CI round will be watched and reported directly."
